irewall on node1 (Alpine Linux) that accepts SSH (22) and TCP 8080, allows loopback/established traffic and ICMP echo, and rejects all other inbound connections with icmp-port-unreachable. Rules were saved via OpenRC (/etc/iptables/rules-save, /etc/iptables/rules6-save) and the iptables/ip6tables services were added to the default runlevel. Verified functionally before and after a full node reboot (new boot_id confirmed a real restart), with firewall rules, service state, and SSH all recovering automatically and correctly.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS (Alpine 3.23) and confirmed no firewall/iptables was installed\",\"Installed iptables and ip6tables packages via apk\",\"Configured INPUT chain: ACCEPT lo, ACCEPT ESTABLISHED/RELATED, ACCEPT tcp/22, ACCEPT tcp/8080, ACCEPT icmp echo-request, REJECT all else, policy DROP (mirrored for ip6tables)\",\"Persisted rules with /etc/init.d/iptables save and /etc/init.d/ip6tables save, added both services to the default OpenRC runlevel, started both services\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and functional proof (8080 allowed, SSH allowed, arbitrary port 9999 rejected)\",\"Issued native reboot on node1, polled until exec access returned\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed (new value after reboot), confirming a genuine restart\",\"Re-verified firewall rules were auto-restored, iptables/ip6tables services started, sshd running, and re-ran functional port tests (8080 allowed, 22 allowed, 9999 rejected) matching baseline\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Persistent firewall installed and enabled on boot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6cfb81c85437450e\",\"cmd-19a353537dd64b63\",\"cmd-ac6255a512044d16\",\"cmd-23d79fa4d4d84d70\"],\"summary\":\"iptables/ip6tables packages installed, rules saved to /etc/iptables/rules-save and rules6-save, services added to default runlevel and started\"},{\"requirement\":\"SSH permitted, TCP 8080 permitted, unrelated inbound rejected (pre-reboot baseline)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3a47f49a8c6942c5\",\